# Force revalidation on every HTML request.
#
# Why this exists (added Aug 20, 2026):
# insidethenumber.com was serving stale HTML from Cloudflare's edge cache
# for hours after a successful deploy, while the underlying
# edge-report.insidethenumber-itn.workers.dev URL served the correct new
# content immediately. On Aug 20 the daily routine pushed the day's picks
# at 10:51am and the public site was STILL showing the previous day's Pick
# of the Day at 3:30pm. Adding a cache-busting query string returned the
# fresh page, which confirmed it was edge caching rather than a failed deploy.
#
# max-age=0 + must-revalidate lets Cloudflare keep a copy but forces it to
# revalidate against the origin before serving, so a new deploy is picked up
# immediately instead of sitting behind a stale cached copy.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Images are public assets anyway; allowing cross-origin reads lets us pull
# them into third-party admin uploaders (beehiiv) programmatically instead of
# hand-uploading branding on every rebrand.
/*.png
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
